GX FIFO translation fast paths (aurora_set_fifo_fast_paths, on by default)

The FIFO worker is the 60 fps limit on the Switch (docs/FPS60_PLAN.md; patch 0020's profile). Two
paths with the same output (byte-identical shots on the Mac), Aurora's own kept behind
aurora_set_fifo_fast_paths(false) for A/B checks:

- Pipeline lookups memoised for the frame by (pipeline config, render target layout): a draw state
  seen earlier in the frame reuses its shader info and pipeline ref instead of build_shader_info,
  the pipeline cache's two config hashes, two locks and the creation callback's config copy (a
  heap allocation). Each state still goes through pipeline_ref once a frame (remembered for the
  cache, promoted while it compiles).
- Merged primitives (most of the stream: display lists of short strips) write their indices straight
  into the frame's index buffer (gfx::map_indices) instead of a staging buffer copied in.

